      "nets": ["+5V"],
      "observed": "The LM1117-5.0 output rail +5V is bypassed only by C1, which is listed as 100nF; the SPICE deck also models it as `C1 +5V 0 100n`.",
      "expected": "For the LM1117 linear regulator, standard practice and the part's datasheet require a larger output capacitor (typically at least 10 µF) for stability; a 100 nF ceramic-only output capacitor is too small for the regulator's output capacitor role.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\")\n      (value \"100nF\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"U2\")\n      (value \"LM1117-5.0\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\") ... (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\")"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C1 +5V 0 100n"}
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V rail may become unstable or oscillate, potentially causing MCU resets or erratic fan-control behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity and most component identities look internally consistent for an ATtiny fan controller, but the LM1117-5.0 output rail has only a 100 nF capacitor, which is too small for the regulator's required output bypass/stability capacitor."
}

